Bad science? Whenever I dip into sci.physics.fusion I am unconvinced
by the latest supposed calorimetric proof.

As to the other things, let me again state that I never claimed
science has ended, that nothing new remains to be done. I argued about
rates, so anecdotal citations of things still needing explanation
don't prove my points, or Nick's points, one way or another.

(I've elided Nick's listing of more recent technological and
scientific innovations. For the same reason.)

> Tim, your theory implies a huge degradation in the human intellect
> during the course of the twentieth century, specifically it implies
> that the garbage/content ratio has increased by more than an order of
